export anchor ProNLEStyle:
    number: 354
    screen: VideoEditor
    name: Pro NLE
    idea: A professional dark grey editing room, four tight panels butted together on a near black frame, tabbed headers, 12px type, and precise yellow timecode as the one voice that speaks loudly.
    base: dark
    palette:
        frame: #0f0f10, the near black frame between panels and the page
        panel: #232325, panel bodies, inspector and bin rows
        header: #1c1c1e, tab strips, ruler and track lanes
        trackHead: #2a2a2d, track header cells and transport buttons
        rule: #38383b, row rules and field borders
        ink: #e6e6e6, text
        muted: #a8a8a8, labels, inactive tabs and meta
        timecode: #ffd84d, timecode, active tab rule, Export and focus
        value: #8fb8ff, scrubbable inspector values and media icons
        videoClip: #35557a, video clips
        titleClip: #6a4c93, title clips
        audioClip: #2c6448, audio clips
        clipEdge: #8fb0d8, the light 1px edge that outlines video clips, with lilac and green twins for titles and audio
        playhead: #d63a2f, playhead flag and line
        marker: #5ad1a8, the cut to logo marker flag
    type:
        One system sans stack, system-ui, Segoe UI, Roboto, Helvetica Neue,
        Arial, and a mono stack, ui-monospace, SF Mono, Menlo, Consolas.
        Base 12px at 1.45. The big timecode is mono 18px at 600 in yellow,
        the duration mono 13px, tab labels 12px at 600, clip labels 11px,
        ruler and bin durations mono 10px to 12px. The title card on the
        monitor is 30px light weight.
    layout:
        A one line menu bar holds a yellow square B, Brightwork Cut, Launch
        teaser with 1080p and 24 fps, then the render readout with an empty
        circle, Render 0% and not started beside a thin bar, and a yellow
        Export button. Below, four panels butt together on a black frame
        with 2px gutters. The left panel is a tabbed bin table with columns
        Name, Duration as full timecode and Type, each row led by a film or
        bars icon. The centre is the program monitor with a dashed safe
        area, the title card, then the yellow current timecode on the left,
        five square transport buttons in the middle and the duration on the
        right. The right panel is Effect controls with grouped rows Motion,
        Opacity and Transition, values in blue mono with a dotted underline.
        The timeline spans the full width with a 112px track header column,
        track ids V2, V1, A1 and A2 with names and an eye or speaker icon, a
        ruler in timecode every 10 seconds, solid clips in steel blue,
        purple and green with a light edge, the selected title clip with a
        white outline and the word selected, a red playhead flag reading 18s
        and a green flag marker labelled cut to logo. Below 1080px the bin
        moves under the monitor. At phone width the bin and inspector hide,
        transport buttons grow to 44px, track headers shrink to the ids and
        every other ruler label hides.
    spacing: A 4px base. Panels touch with 2px black gutters, rows are 24px, track lanes 38px.
    density: High. Bin, monitor, inspector and a full four track timeline share one screen.
    corners: 2px on buttons, clips and the logo. Panels are square.
    borders: 1px black separators, 1px #38383b row rules and a 1px light edge on every clip. No outlines on panels.
    shadows: None. Depth comes from three grey steps.
    icons:
        Thin 1.4 stroke line icons at 14px. Film frame for video, vertical
        bars for audio, eye and speaker on tracks, filled triangle for play.
        The marker is a pentagon flag and the playhead a notched red tag.
    focus: A 2px timecode yellow outline offset 1px on every control.
    tone: Terse professional labels such as Program, Effect controls and 5 items.
